From cbb9ed5136b09d3ae437321d3b1883f613ae51a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:48:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] CI: don't put R's lib directory on LD_LIBRARY_PATH

On Linux, JuliaCall's first-run install of RCall.jl and Suppressor.jl
(install_dependency.jl, run as a Julia subprocess) segfaulted with
status 139, so every cs_setup() failed with "Package Suppressor not
found". The step putting $(R RHOME)/lib on LD_LIBRARY_PATH, copied from
RCall.jl's CI, makes every Julia process load R's bundled libraries
first; users' setups (e.g. Ubuntu with system R) work without it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YAJEP7UjxoayyA9FXy4GeK
---
 .github/workflows/julia-integration.yaml | 5 -----
 1 file changed, 5 deletions(-)

